// ==========================================================================
// Axi_Mux -- merges four AXI masters onto the DDR3 controller
// ==========================================================================
// Slave port 0 : SoC DDR master       (full AXI4)
// Slave port 1 : bitblt read source   (AR/R only -- AW/W/B tied off)
// Slave port 2 : bitblt read dest     (AR/R only -- AW/W/B tied off)
// Slave port 3 : bitblt write engine  (AW/W/B only -- AR/R tied off)
//
// The engines only implement the half of AXI4 they need, but Axi_Mux expects a
// complete port on every slave, so the unused halves are tied to constants.
// Each *_W_ID must equal the corresponding AW_ID: Axi_Mux uses the ID to tell
// in-flight transactions from different channels apart.
//
// LOCK is 2 bits inside Axi_Mux but 1 bit on the SoC and the DDR3 controller,
// so it is zero-extended on the way in and truncated on the way out. Both are
// written out explicitly -- see the note near the wire declarations.
// ==========================================================================
